<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parlement of Paris</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Parlement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> was the highest court of justice of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, developed from the king's court in the thirteenth century and housed in the royal palace on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ile-de-la-cite">Île de la Cité</a>. Its jurisdiction covered much of northern and central France, and it heard appeals from great fiefs such as Aquitaine. It also registered royal laws, which gave it political weight, until it was abolished in 1790 during the Revolution.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/parlement-of-paris.jpg" alt="Parlement of Paris" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pierre Louis Dumesnil · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lit_de_justice_tenu_par_Louis_XV.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
